---
const signals = [
  {
    date: "24 Aug 2026",
    title: "Acquisition: ADLATUS Robotics",
    category: "Portfolio Expansion",
    summary:
      "NEURA acquired ADLATUS Robotics, adding hundreds of installed autonomous cleaning systems, navigation technology, and application know-how.",
    why:
      "More products and inherited application knowledge may increase the challenge of making technical expertise available across sales and service teams.",
    source:
      "https://neura-robotics.com/de/neura-ubernimmt-adlatus-robotics/",
  },
  {
    date: "13 Aug 2026",
    title: "Acquisition: Bosch Rexroth ACTIVE Shuttle",
    category: "Portfolio Expansion",
    summary:
      "NEURA is integrating Bosch Rexroth's ACTIVE Shuttle into its Physical AI ecosystem.",
    why:
      "Expanding the product portfolio may increase configuration complexity and application-specific questions during the sales process.",
    source:
      "https://neura-robotics.com/de/neura-robotics-ubernimmt-active-shuttle/",
  },
  {
    date: "22 Jul 2026",
    title: "Global Training Expansion",
    category: "Knowledge Scaling",
    summary:
      "NEURA expanded its Physical AI training network with a new NEURA Gym at RWTH Aachen.",
    why:
      "Scaling training suggests that distributing technical knowledge effectively is strategically important.",
    source: "https://neura-robotics.com/de/news/",
  },
  {
    date: "10 Jun 2026",
    title: "Major Growth Financing",
    category: "Growth",
    summary:
      "NEURA announced financing of up to $1.4 billion to accelerate its Physical AI platform.",
    why:
      "Rapid organizational and product scaling can create pressure to scale technical sales knowledge more efficiently.",
    source: "https://neura-robotics.com/news/",
  },
  {
    date: "21 Apr 2026",
    title: "Strategic AWS Partnership",
    category: "Ecosystem",
    summary:
      "NEURA and AWS announced a strategic partnership around the Neuraverse, robotics training, and international market expansion.",
    why:
      "More partners, markets, and deployments can increase the number of people who need access to accurate technical application knowledge.",
    source:
      "https://neura-robotics.com/de/neura-robotics-und-amazon-web-services-starten-strategische-partnerschaft/",
  },
];

const scoreBreakdown = [
  {
    label: "Technical product complexity",
    score: 19,
    max: 20,
    reason:
      "Robotics, software, integrations, and multiple application environments create substantial technical complexity.",
  },
  {
    label: "Application engineering dependency",
    score: 18,
    max: 20,
    reason:
      "Robotics deployments typically require application-specific technical expertise during evaluation, configuration, and implementation.",
  },
  {
    label: "International / partner sales",
    score: 17,
    max: 20,
    reason:
      "NEURA is expanding through partnerships, ecosystems, and international activity.",
  },
  {
    label: "Growth and change signals",
    score: 18,
    max: 20,
    reason:
      "Recent acquisitions, financing, partnerships, and training expansion indicate significant organizational change.",
  },
  {
    label: "Evidence of current pain",
    score: 9,
    max: 20,
    reason:
      "There are strong structural indicators, but no direct public evidence confirming an application-engineering bottleneck.",
  },
];

const pressureIndicators = [
  {
    label: "Growth pressure",
    value: "High",
    explanation:
      "Acquisitions, funding, partnerships, and international expansion are happening simultaneously.",
  },
  {
    label: "Knowledge complexity",
    value: "High",
    explanation:
      "Multiple robot platforms, software layers, applications, and newly acquired technologies increase the amount of expertise that must be shared.",
  },
  {
    label: "GTM urgency",
    value: "Medium–High",
    explanation:
      "Rapid expansion increases the importance of enabling commercial teams and partners without scaling expert headcount at the same rate.",
  },
];

const totalScore = scoreBreakdown.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.score, 0);
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />

    <meta
      name="viewport"
      content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"
    />

    <meta
      name="description"
      content="A GTM experiment exploring whether public signals can identify potential Bardin opportunities in the German industrial market."
    />

    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />

    <title>Bardin × Germany — NEURA Robotics GTM Experiment</title>

    <style>
      :root {
        --bg: #f5f6f3;
        --card: #ffffff;
        --text: #10110f;
        --muted: #62665f;
        --border: #dfe3da;

        --bardin-green: #b7ff2a;
        --bardin-green-soft: #efffd0;
        --bardin-green-mid: #8fda18;
        --bardin-green-dark: #536f10;

        --dark: #11120f;

        --accent: var(--bardin-green-dark);
        --accent-soft: var(--bardin-green-soft);
      }

      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        font-family:
          Inter,
          ui-sans-serif,
          system-ui,
          -apple-system,
          BlinkMacSystemFont,
          "Segoe UI",
          sans-serif;
        background: var(--bg);
        color: var(--text);
        line-height: 1.55;
      }

      a {
        color: inherit;
      }

      main {
        width: min(1100px, calc(100% - 32px));
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 56px 0 80px;
      }

      /* HERO */

      .hero {
        position: relative;
        overflow: hidden;
        padding: 38px;
        margin-bottom: 32px;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 24px;
        background: var(--dark);
        color: white;
      }

      .hero::after {
        content: "";
        position: absolute;
        width: 240px;
        height: 240px;
        right: -90px;
        top: -90px;
        border-radius: 50%;
        background: var(--bardin-green);
        opacity: 0.14;
      }

      .eyebrow {
        display: inline-block;
        margin-bottom: 16px;
        padding: 7px 11px;
        border-radius: 999px;
        background: var(--bardin-green);
        color: #10110f;
        font-size: 13px;
        font-weight: 800;
      }

      h1 {
        position: relative;
        z-index: 1;
        margin: 0;
        font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
        line-height: 0.98;
        letter-spacing: -0.05em;
      }

      .subtitle {
        position: relative;
        z-index: 1;
        max-width: 780px;
        margin-top: 18px;
        color: #d6dad0;
        font-size: 1.1rem;
      }

      .meta-row {
        position: relative;
        z-index: 1;
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 10px;
        margin-top: 24px;
      }

      .meta-pill {
        padding: 8px 12px;
        border: 1px solid #30332c;
        border-radius: 999px;
        background: #181a16;
        color: #f1f2ee;
        font-size: 14px;
      }

      /* SECTIONS */

      section {
        margin-top: 48px;
      }

      h2 {
        position: relative;
        margin: 0 0 18px;
        padding-left: 14px;
        font-size: 1.5rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.025em;
      }

      h2::before {
        content: "";
        position: absolute;
        left: 0;
        top: 0.18em;
        bottom: 0.18em;
        width: 4px;
        border-radius: 4px;
        background: var(--bardin-green);
      }

      h3 {
        letter-spacing: -0.015em;
      }

      .section-note {
        max-width: 720px;
        margin: -8px 0 20px;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.95rem;
      }

      /* AGENT FLOW */

      .agent-label {
        margin: 0 0 9px;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 12px;
        font-weight: 800;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      }

      .agent-flow {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr;
        gap: 14px;
        align-items: center;
        padding: 22px;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 18px;
        background: var(--card);
      }

      .flow-stat {
        text-align: center;
      }

      .flow-number {
        display: block;
        font-size: 2.2rem;
        font-weight: 800;
        line-height: 1;
        letter-spacing: -0.05em;
      }

      .flow-label {
        display: block;
        margin-top: 7px;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.9rem;
      }

      .flow-arrow {
        color: var(--bardin-green-dark);
        font-size: 1.6rem;
        font-weight: 900;
      }

      /* GENERAL GRID */

      .grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
        gap: 16px;
      }

      .card {
        padding: 22px;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 18px;
        background: var(--card);
      }

      /* WHY NOW */

      .pressure-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
        gap: 14px;
      }

      .pressure-card {
        position: relative;
        overflow: hidden;
        padding: 20px;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 16px;
        background: var(--card);
      }

      .pressure-card::before {
        content: "";
        position: absolute;
        left: 0;
        right: 0;
        top: 0;
        height: 5px;
        background: var(--bardin-green);
      }

      .pressure-label {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 13px;
        font-weight: 700;
      }

      .pressure-value {
        display: block;
        margin: 6px 0 10px;
        font-size: 1.5rem;
        font-weight: 800;
      }

      .pressure-explanation {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.92rem;
      }

      /* SNAPSHOT */

      .snapshot-card {
        position: relative;
      }

      .snapshot-card strong {
        display: block;
        margin-bottom: 5px;
        color: var(--bardin-green-dark);
        font-size: 13px;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      }

      .snapshot-card span {
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        font-weight: 700;
      }

      /* SIGNALS */

      .signal-card {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 12px;
        transition:
          transform 0.18s ease,
          border-color 0.18s ease;
      }

      .signal-card:hover {
        transform: translateY(-2px);
        border-color: #c5d8a6;
      }

      .signal-top {
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 12px;
      }

      .signal-date {
        font-size: 13px;
        color: var(--muted);
      }

      .signal-category {
        padding: 5px 8px;
        border-radius: 999px;
        background: var(--bardin-green-soft);
        color: #40570b;
        font-size: 11px;
        font-weight: 800;
      }

      .signal-card h3 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 1.15rem;
      }

      .signal-card p {
        margin: 0;
      }

      .why {
        padding: 14px;
        border-left: 3px solid var(--bardin-green);
        border-radius: 10px;
        background: #f8faF4;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
      }

      .source-link {
        margin-top: auto;
        padding-top: 4px;
        color: var(--bardin-green-dark);
        font-size: 14px;
        font-weight: 800;
        text-decoration: none;
      }

      .source-link:hover {
        text-decoration: underline;
      }

      /* SCORE */

      .score-layout {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 260px 1fr;
        gap: 20px;
        align-items: start;
      }

      .score-box {
        padding: 28px;
        border-top: 5px solid var(--bardin-green);
        border-radius: 20px;
        background: var(--dark);
        color: white;
      }

      .score-number {
        display: block;
        color: var(--bardin-green);
        font-size: 4rem;
        line-height: 1;
        font-weight: 800;
        letter-spacing: -0.06em;
      }

      .score-label {
        margin-top: 8px;
        color: #c8ccd2;
      }

      .score-status {
        display: inline-block;
        margin-top: 18px;
        padding: 7px 10px;
        border-radius: 999px;
        background: var(--bardin-green);
        color: var(--dark);
        font-size: 13px;
        font-weight: 800;
      }

      .score-items {
        display: grid;
        gap: 12px;
      }

      .score-item {
        padding: 16px;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 14px;
        background: var(--card);
      }

      .score-top {
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 16px;
        margin-bottom: 5px;
      }

      .score-top strong {
        font-size: 0.98rem;
      }

      .score-value {
        color: var(--bardin-green-dark);
        font-weight: 800;
      }

      .score-reason {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.92rem;
      }

      /* HYPOTHESIS */

      .hypothesis {
        padding: 28px;
        border-left: 5px solid var(--bardin-green);
        border-radius: 14px;
        background: var(--card);
        font-size: 1.2rem;
      }

      .hypothesis strong {
        display: block;
        margin-bottom: 10px;
        color: var(--bardin-green-dark);
        font-size: 13px;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.07em;
      }

      /* DISCOVERY QUESTION */

      .question-card {
        padding: 30px;
        border-radius: 18px;
        background: var(--dark);
        color: white;
      }

      .question-card .label {
        margin-bottom: 12px;
        color: var(--bardin-green);
        font-size: 13px;
        font-weight: 800;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      }

      .question-card blockquote {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 1.35rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        line-height: 1.4;
      }

      /* ACTIONS */

      .action-list {
        display: grid;
        gap: 12px;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        list-style: none;
      }

      .action-list li {
        position: relative;
        padding: 18px 18px 18px 24px;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 14px;
        background: var(--card);
      }

      .action-list li::before {
        content: "";
        position: absolute;
        left: 0;
        top: 0;
        bottom: 0;
        width: 5px;
        border-radius: 14px 0 0 14px;
        background: var(--bardin-green);
      }

      /* METHOD */

      .method {
        padding: 20px;
        border: 1px dashed #b8c49f;
        border-radius: 14px;
        background: #fafcf6;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.92rem;
      }

      footer {
        margin-top: 64px;
        padding-top: 24px;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 13px;
      }

      @media (max-width: 760px) {
        main {
          width: min(100% - 22px, 1100px);
          padding-top: 24px;
        }

        .hero {
          padding: 26px 22px;
        }

        .grid,
        .score-layout,
        .pressure-grid {
          grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }

        .agent-flow {
          grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }

        .flow-arrow {
          transform: rotate(90deg);
          text-align: center;
        }

        .score-box {
          padding: 22px;
        }

        .score-number {
          font-size: 3.2rem;
        }

        .question-card {
          padding: 24px;
        }

        .question-card blockquote {
          font-size: 1.15rem;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <main>

      <!-- HERO -->

      <header class="hero">
        <span class="eyebrow">Private GTM Experiment</span>

        <h1>Bardin × Germany</h1>

        <p class="subtitle">
          Can public market signals identify industrial companies where
          deployment complexity, technical knowledge bottlenecks, and engineering
          escalation create a strong opportunity for Bardin?
        </p>

        <div class="meta-row">
          <span class="meta-pill">Pilot account: NEURA Robotics</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Market: Germany / DACH</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Last reviewed: 27 Aug 2026</span>
        </div>
      </header>


      <!-- AGENT WORKFLOW -->

      <section>
        <p class="agent-label">Agent-assisted GTM research workflow</p>

        <div class="agent-flow">
          <div class="flow-stat">
            <span class="flow-number">{signals.length}</span>
            <span class="flow-label">signals analyzed</span>
          </div>

          <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>

          <div class="flow-stat">
            <span class="flow-number">1</span>
            <span class="flow-label">pain hypothesis</span>
          </div>

          <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>

          <div class="flow-stat">
            <span class="flow-number">4</span>
            <span class="flow-label">recommended actions</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>


      <!-- WHY NOW -->

      <section>
        <h2>Why Now?</h2>

        <p class="section-note">
          A quick interpretation of whether recent public signals make this
          account especially interesting for Bardin right now.
        </p>

        <div class="pressure-grid">
          {
            pressureIndicators.map((indicator) => (
              <article class="pressure-card">
                <div class="pressure-label">{indicator.label}</div>
                <span class="pressure-value">{indicator.value}</span>
                <div class="pressure-explanation">
                  {indicator.explanation}
                </div>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </section>


      <!-- SNAPSHOT -->

      <section>
        <h2>Account Snapshot</h2>

        <div class="grid">
          <div class="card snapshot-card">
            <strong>Company</strong>
            <span>NEURA Robotics</span>
          </div>

          <div class="card snapshot-card">
            <strong>Location</strong>
            <span>Germany</span>
          </div>

          <div class="card snapshot-card">
            <strong>Industry</strong>
            <span>Robotics / Physical AI</span>
          </div>

          <div class="card snapshot-card">
            <strong>Why relevant</strong>
            <span>
              Complex products, application-specific engineering, rapid expansion,
              and a growing partner ecosystem.
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>


      <!-- SIGNALS -->

      <section>
        <h2>Recent Signals</h2>

        <p class="section-note">
          Public evidence first. Interpretation is shown separately so that
          observable facts are not confused with inferred customer pain.
        </p>

        <div class="grid">
          {
            signals.map((signal) => (
              <article class="card signal-card">

                <div class="signal-top">
                  <span class="signal-date">{signal.date}</span>
                  <span class="signal-category">{signal.category}</span>
                </div>

                <h3>{signal.title}</h3>

                <p>{signal.summary}</p>

                <div class="why">
                  <strong>Possible GTM implication:</strong><br />
                  {signal.why}
                </div>

                <a
                  class="source-link"
                  href={signal.source}
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                >
                  View source ↗
                </a>

              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </section>


      <!-- ICP SCORE -->

      <section>
        <h2>Bardin ICP Fit</h2>

        <p class="section-note">
          This score measures structural fit with Bardin's use case.
          It is not a probability that NEURA is experiencing a confirmed problem.
        </p>

        <div class="score-layout">

          <div class="score-box">
            <span class="score-number">{totalScore}</span>
            <div class="score-label">out of 100</div>
            <span class="score-status">Strong potential fit</span>
          </div>

          <div class="score-items">
            {
              scoreBreakdown.map((item) => (
                <div class="score-item">

                  <div class="score-top">
                    <strong>{item.label}</strong>
                    <span class="score-value">
                      {item.score}/{item.max}
                    </span>
                  </div>

                  <div class="score-reason">
                    {item.reason}
                  </div>

                </div>
              ))
            }
          </div>

        </div>
      </section>


      <!-- HYPOTHESIS -->

      <section>
        <h2>Pain Hypothesis</h2>

        <div class="hypothesis">

          <strong>Hypothesis — not confirmed fact</strong>

          NEURA's rapid portfolio, ecosystem, and international expansion may make
          it increasingly difficult to distribute application-specific technical
          knowledge across sales, partners, service teams, and newly integrated
          business units without repeatedly involving scarce technical experts.

        </div>
      </section>


      <!-- DISCOVERY QUESTION -->

      <section>
        <h2>Best Discovery Question</h2>

        <div class="question-card">

          <div class="label">
            Question to validate the hypothesis
          </div>

          <blockquote>
            “When a new customer or partner needs to configure a robot for a
            specific application, how much of that process still depends on
            getting one of your application engineers involved?”
          </blockquote>

        </div>
      </section>


      <!-- ACTIONS -->

      <section>
        <h2>Recommended Next Actions</h2>

        <ul class="action-list">

          <li>
            <strong>1. Identify the likely buyer</strong><br />
            Find leaders responsible for Application Engineering, Sales Engineering,
            Technical Sales, or Partner Enablement.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>2. Validate the bottleneck</strong><br />
            Determine whether repetitive technical questions are slowing sales,
            partner enablement, or consuming application-engineering capacity.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>3. Map where technical knowledge lives</strong><br />
            Understand whether answers currently depend on individual experts,
            product documentation, internal systems, or informal conversations.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>4. Test one narrow Bardin use case</strong><br />
            Select one product family or application area where commercial teams
            repeatedly require engineering support and evaluate whether that
            knowledge can become reusable.
          </li>

        </ul>
      </section>


      <!-- METHOD -->

      <section>
        <h2>Research Method</h2>

        <div class="method">
          Public company signals → structured research → relevance classification →
          ICP scoring → pain hypothesis → human review → recommended discovery action.

          <br /><br />

          The objective is not to claim knowledge of an internal problem, but to
          prioritize accounts where public evidence suggests that a relevant problem
          is worth validating.
        </div>
      </section>


      <footer>
        AI-assisted research · Human reviewed · Public sources linked ·
        Hypotheses are intended for validation, not presented as confirmed customer pain.
      </footer>

    </main>
  </body>
</html>
